-- title:
--   Raised local component at level Nq with θ̄(U_q)=0
-- statement:
--   Fix non-zero naturals $N$ and $q$ with $q$ prime and $q \mid N$, together with two instances of the predicate [`CohCarrier.LevelLE`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L330) for the pair $(N, Nq)$ with full unit subgroups $\top$ at both levels and degrees $1$ and $q$ respectively (each asserting $N \mid Nq$, that the degree divides $(Nq)/N$, and that reduction carries $\top$ into $\top$); fix a set $S$ of naturals and a Noetherian local ring $\mathcal{O}$ that is adically complete for its maximal ideal, with residue field $k =$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField` $\mathcal{O}$. For a level $M$, [`CohCarrier.Gen M S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) is the inductive type of generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid M$), $U_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \mid M$) and $\langle d \rangle$ ($d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$), and [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) sends $T_\ell$ and $U_\ell$ to `heckeTL` (precomposition with `conjL` followed by the transfer `coresAdd`) and $\langle d \rangle$ to `diamondL`, all acting on $H^1(M, \top, \mathcal{O}) = \operatorname{Hom}(\mathrm{Additive}\,\Gamma_\top(M), \mathcal{O})$. Hypotheses `hcomm`, `hcomm'` assert that these operators commute pairwise at levels $N$ and $Nq$. Given systems of residual eigenvalues $\bar\theta$ on `Gen N S` and $\bar\theta'$ on `Gen (N*q) S` with values in $k$, assume: $\bar\theta'(T_\ell) = \bar\theta(T_\ell)$ for $\ell$ prime, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid Nq$; $\bar\theta'(U_\ell) = \bar\theta(U_\ell)$ for $\ell$ prime dividing $N$ with $\ell \neq q$; $\bar\theta'(U_q) = 0$; and $\bar\theta'(\langle d \rangle) = 1$ for all $d$. Assume further an [`IharaLemma.IdempotentSplitting`](def/IharaLemma_IdempotentSplitting.html#L7) $Sp$ of the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra `opSubalgebra` of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}} H^1(N, \top, \mathcal{O})$ generated by the operators (a family of complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,n$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting all maximal ideals, with $e_i \in \mathfrak{m}_j$ exactly when $i \neq j$), an index $i_0$, and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\pi_k$ from the corner ring $e_{i_0} \mathbb{T} e_{i_0}$ to $k$ with $\pi_k(e_{i_0}\,\mathrm{op}(g)\,e_{i_0}) = \bar\theta(g)$ for every generator $g$. The final hypothesis is that the level-raising operator $\iota_q^* \circ U_q - q\,\iota_1^*$, built from `iDegL` and `heckeTL` at $q$, is injective on the corner submodule $e_{i_0} \cdot H^1(N, \top, \mathcal{O})$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an idempotent splitting $Sp'$ of the corresponding operator subalgebra at level $Nq$, an index $i_0'$, and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\pi_{k}'$ from its corner ring to $k$ with $\pi_k'(e_{i_0'}\,\mathrm{op}(g)\,e_{i_0'}) = \bar\theta'(g)$ for every generator $g$ of `Gen (N*q) S`.
--
--   This is the level-raising step at a prime $q$ already dividing the level: from a local component of the Hecke algebra at level $N$ cut out by a residual eigensystem $\bar\theta$, on which the operator $\iota_q^* U_q - q\,\iota_1^*$ is injective, one obtains a local component at level $Nq$ realising the eigensystem $\bar\theta'$ that agrees with $\bar\theta$ away from $q$ and has $U_q$ acting by $0$. It is used in the construction of the chain of corner realisations underlying the auxiliary-level Hecke algebras of the modularity-lifting argument.
